'use strict';
// data/voice/dialog-ch8.js — Chapter 8 spoken dialogue clips, keyed 'voice|exact text' (data/dialog-cast.js). Built from the
// Chapter Voice Baker with claude/voice-merge-dialog.js; do not hand-edit.
Object.assign(DIALOG_CLIPS.clips,{"tom|\"Also every oven on 2nd Ave just went cold. At the same time. At noon. Come home.\"":"","tom|I did not fly here to serve forty people raw dough.":"","tom|Bready Mercury’s dough has been rising since Thursday. Forty loaves. It needs a five hundred degree oven.":"","tnb|Hi. Love you. Do not panic. Touch your stove.":"","tom|...I have not been home yet.":"","tnb|Right. Well, it is cold. Everybody’s is cold. I tried to light yours. The flame LEANED, babe. Sideways. Toward the boulevard. Like it wanted to leave.":"","penny|Tom. Good. Neighborhood Watch Captain, potluck committee chair. Forty RSVPs. Thirty-nine dishes. One bread guy.":"","tom|Did you call the gas company?":"","tom|\"Babe. Potluck is TONIGHT. Forty people. You are on bread.\"":"","penny|Every pilot light on 2nd Avenue went out at noon. Every one. Including mine. I had a casserole IN there.":"","penny|They said it is the weekend. I said it is the POTLUCK. They hung up. I have filed a report. With myself.":"","tnb|I have wanted to go in there since I MOVED here.":"","olivia|Tom! Can you take Nara? She will not eat. Her dinner is cold, so she will not eat it. Michael warmed it in his hands. She still will not eat it.":"","tnb|East. Toward the end of the boulevard. Babe. The old Car Barn. Division Nine. The streetcars ran out of there until 1963.":"","penny|The barn? It has been chained up for sixty years. Here. Committee key. I am the committee. We are closing the boulevard for the tables. Bread by six.":"","olivia|Bring her back fed! Please! Michael, Isla is eating the lasagna. It is a brick. She is eating a brick.":"","tnb|Oh. Oh, babe. Look at it. The tracks are still in the floor. The time clock. The crew bench. I am going to cry a little.":"","tom|It is freezing in here. It is seventy-four degrees outside.":"","tom|Those are pilot lights. The whole block’s pilot lights. Something down here is collecting them.":"","tnb|And some of them got stuck. Look. The Paint Shop, the Machine Shop, the Lunchroom. Something in each one is hogging one.":"","tnb|Wow. Okay. Big mood, buddy.":"","tom|That flame is a gumbo. Forty years of gumbo. Hand it over.":"","tnb|Okay. Up. Everybody up. Hot cocoa later. Lots of it.":"","tnb|It dried out a little. Look. It is almost fluffy. It is a blanket again.":"","tom|A pilot light. A tiny blue flame, floating right there. That is Mr. Washington’s stove. That is the gumbo.":"","tom|You can fix anything.":"","tnb|That is three, babe. And that little steam motor by the turntable has three empty burners. Three. I can fix that.":"","skeeter|Ironbelly asked for the flames, so I carried them. I am a delivery draft.":"","tnb|I can fix most things. I fixed your dishwasher with a butter knife.":"","skeeter|Wooooo. Pfft. Pfft. Pfft. That was me. I blew them all out. Every stove on the block.":"","tom|Who is Ironbelly.":"","tom|Ironbelly. Somebody named Ironbelly wanted every flame on 2nd Ave.":"","skeeter|Wooooo. I said nothing. I am just air.":"","tnb|That is either a boat or a stove. In a car barn, babe, it is a stove.":"","tom|A pilot light. A tiny blue flame, floating right there. That is Olivia’s stove. That is the lasagna.":"","tnb|Babe. It is her. It is Nara as a lunchbox.":"","toad|Ew. EW. Who are you. What is that. Is that a dog? Ew. Is that BREAD? Bread is the worst. Bread TOUCHES things.":"","toad|...Fine. FINE. Take it. I will try a bite of something. Later. Maybe. If it is warm. And not touching.":"","tom|That flame is my oven. My forty loaves. Put it down. No touching, please.":"","tom|A pilot light. A tiny blue flame, floating right there. That is Tom’s own stove. That is the forty loaves.":"","tnb|She would not eat her own dinner. She ate YOUR dinner.":"","tom|Tom takes out the sandwich he packed for himself. Turkey, mustard, his own sourdough. He puts it on his own plate. He sits down.":"","tom|A note taped inside the lid: FOR THE NEXT SHIFT. HAVE A GOOD RUN. BOOKER W.":"","tom|It was on my plate. That is the rule. Food on her plate is suspicious. Food on my plate is a gift.":"","tom|And a picnic basket. Somebody packed it a very long time ago. It is somehow fine.":"","tnb|Babe. Somebody left lunch for the next guy. Sixty years ago. That is the nicest thing I have ever seen in a train yard.":"","tnb|Babe, close a door on it. Any door.":"","tom|Under wardrobe?":"","tnb|Under hero.":"","tnb|Babe. BABE. We turned a turntable. Do you know how many people get to turn a turntable? Like eleven.":"","tnb|Babe. It is warm in here. Like, really warm. Like, opening-the-oven-door warm.":"","bigone|...Who is in my Boiler Room. Nobody comes down here. Not since the last car went out. 1963.":"","bigone|Everybody up there has a little fire. I have been cold for sixty years. I only borrowed some.":"","tom|You took every pilot light on 2nd Avenue.":"","bigone|And look at me. I am WARM again. I am five hundred degrees. Do you know how long it has been since I was five hundred degrees?":"","tnb|Okay. Up. Everybody up. That was hot. That was SO hot.":"","tom|Give the flames back. No touching, please.":"","tnb|Babe, Splash cools her down. Cozy stokes her up, so not too much of that. And she wants somebody to bake something in her. Three times.":"","bigone|...Fine. FINE. Take your little flames back. I will be cold again. I am used to it.":"","tom|Or. Forty loaves. Tonight. You are the only oven on 2nd Ave hot enough.":"","bigone|A potluck. Everybody brings a dish. Nobody ever brings anything to the oven. Nobody has put a single thing in me since 1963.":"","bigone|...Forty? Nobody has asked me for forty anything since 1963. Bring the dough.":"","tnb|Forty loaves, babe. FORTY. They are crackling. Listen to them. They are singing.":"","bigone|That is the crust. That is what crust does when it is done right. Here. Take my peel. Fifty-one years of biscuits. It wants to work again.":"","tom|The sundial. The steamer. The sign-up sheet. My jar. The book from 1952. And now an oven nobody has opened since 1963.":"","tnb|Somebody keeps getting into places nobody gets into. Very neat. Very quiet. Very spooky. I love it. I hate it.":"","tom|Look at the corners. Not a speck of ash on it. Somebody put it there after the fire went out. I am adding it to the list.":"","tnb|Noted, Bernadette.":"","penny|Forty loaves. Six o’clock. On the dot. Potluck committee report: we are a success.":"","olivia|Tom. TOM. Nara is eating. Look at her. She is EATING.":"","washington|Tom. Come here. This was my daddy’s. He drove the 7 line out of that barn for thirty years. Night run. He swore by the biscuits.":"","washington|He would want it on somebody who went back in there and lit that stove. Here.":"","penny|The gumbo is hot. The casserole is hot. Everything is hot. I would like it noted.":"","tom|...Thank you. I will take very good care of it.":"","washington|I know you will. Now stand up straight. He would say that too.":"","michael|Lachlan has eaten three rolls and fallen asleep in the bread basket. I am leaving him there. He is happy.":"","tnb|You know what tonight was, babe? Toast.":"","tom|It works on one level. Barely.":"","tom|A text from Deedee. \"Honey. A letter came for you at our house. Fancy envelope. Gold wax seal with a little clock on it.\"":"","tom|\"It says THE MOON CLUB. Nobody gets invited to the Moon Club. I have lived here forty years. I love you to the moon and back. Call me.\"":"","tom|A little clock. On the seal.":"","olivia|Nara ate! A whole plate! Off your plate, but still! I am counting it!":"","olivia|Michael, Isla has a roll in each hand. That is fine. That is a balanced meal.":"","tnb|Because the bread. And we are TOASTING. It works on two levels.":"","olivia|Did she eat? She will not eat cold food. She will not eat warm food either. She eats off YOUR plate, Tom.":"","michael|Best potluck ever. Lachlan fell asleep in the bread basket.":"","olivia|My lasagna is a brick. A cold lasagna brick. Michael is holding it. He is holding everything.":"","michael|I have Isla, the diaper bag, and a cold lasagna. I am at full capacity.":"","washington|That coat looks right on you. My daddy would say so. Then he would say stand up straight.":"","washington|Forty loaves. I ate four. Do not tell Bernadette.":"","washington|My daddy drove the 7 line out of the old Car Barn. He said the stove down there could warm a whole street.":"","la_woman|My dog ate a whole loaf. I found him. He was under the table. He is always under the table.":"","la_woman|My tamales are cold. My dog is cold. My dog is somewhere. He is probably cold.":"","mudling|Nobody ever finishes me. They pour me, they get busy, they forget.":"","mudling|I am fine. I am FINE. I am exactly room temperature.":"","mudling|Round 2. Still lukewarm.":"","mudling|Round 3. Still lukewarm.":"","mudling|Round 4. Still lukewarm.":"","mudling|Round 5. Still lukewarm.":"","gus|I am blowing leaves. They are frosty. In LA. I have questions.":"","mudling|...somebody made me and walked away.":"","mudling|I was hot once. For about four minutes.":"","mudling|Everybody brings me home. Nobody ever opens me again.":"","mudling|Reheated! Round two!":"","washington|Forty years I have made gumbo for this potluck. Today the stove will not light. The flame just leans. Toward the boulevard.":"","mudling|Round 2. Day 2 in the fridge.":"","mudling|Round 3. Day 3 in the fridge.":"","mudling|Round 4. Day 4 in the fridge.":"","mudling|Round 5. Day 5 in the fridge.":"","mudling|...I was a lasagna. I think. Once.":"","mudling|Somebody said they would eat me tomorrow. That was a long tomorrow.":"","log|They used to throw me over the sparks when the welders worked. I put out every fire in this barn.":"","log|Now there is nothing left to put out. So I put out the fun.":"","log|Round 2. Still damp.":"","log|Round 3. Still damp.":"","log|Round 4. Still damp.":"","log|...why bother. Why bother at all.":"","log|Every spark in here, I put it out. Somebody has to.":"","skeeter|I blew out every pilot light on 2nd Avenue. Pfft. Pfft. Pfft. Very satisfying.":"","skeeter|Ironbelly asked for the flames. I just carried them. I am a delivery draft.":"","skeeter|Woooo! Round two!":"","log|Round 5. Still damp.":"","skeeter|Round 2. Still drafty.":"","skeeter|Round 3. Still drafty.":"","skeeter|Round 4. Still drafty.":"","skeeter|Round 5. Still drafty.":"","skeeter|...wooo. Wooooo. That is me. I am the wooo.":"","log|Why bother? Round two.":"","toad|Ironbelly used to warm every lunch in here. Now everything is cold, and everything is EW.":"","toad|Ew! Round two!":"","toad|Round 2. Still not eating it.":"","toad|Round 3. Still not eating it.":"","toad|Round 4. Still not eating it.":"","skeeter|Close a window. Go on. I will find another one.":"","toad|I do not eat cold food. I do not eat hot food. I do not eat food that TOUCHES.":"","toad|I only eat the crust. No, the middle. No. Neither.":"","toad|...ew. Ew. Is that touching? It is touching. EW.":"","bigone|Biscuits for the night crew. Cornbread on Fridays. Every night from 1912 to 1963.":"","bigone|Everybody has a little fire upstairs. I only borrowed it.":"","bigone|Stoke it! Round two!":"","bigone|Round 2. Still preheating.":"","bigone|Round 3. Still preheating.":"","bigone|Round 4. Still preheating.":"","bigone|Round 5. Still preheating.":"","bigone|...cold. Sixty years cold.":"","bigone|Nobody bakes anything anymore. Not in me.":"","sal|Airport? You JUST landed. Your young man said, and I quote, \"forty loaves, babe.\"":"","sal|I do not know what that means. It sounded serious.":"","log|...Oh. Visitors. Great. I suppose you want that little flame.":"","log|Why bother. It is just going to go out. Everything goes out eventually.":"","tnb|Okay. Burner one. Burner two. Burner three. Righty tighty. Lefty... no, righty. Righty tighty.":"","tnb|On the day of the POTLUCK, though.":"","tnb|Steam. We have STEAM, babe. I fixed a hundred-year-old turntable motor. I am going to put this on my resume.":"","mudling|Do not smell me. I am serious. Do not.":"","bigone|I am Old Ironbelly. 1912. Cast iron, all the way through. Biscuits for the night crew, every night, for fifty-one years. Cornbread on Fridays.":"","tnb|The Moon Club. Babe. That is a secret society. I have seen this movie. Several times. It never goes well for the tall one.":"","toad|Round 5. Still not eating it.":""});
Object.assign(DIALOG_CLIPS.voices,{"tom":{"voice_id":"cjVigY5qzO86Huf0OWal","name":"Eric - Smooth, Trustworthy","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"tnb":{"voice_id":"QPmHuIriDGOvu1d9U7wn","name":"SuperDale - a mid-age voice & Friendly  (male, middle_aged, us midwest, informative_educational)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"penny":{"voice_id":"C0jocNoR6bwrjLXwelto","name":"AoT Penny","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her forties with a fast-talking, bright, enthusiastic American saleswoman voice. Quick patter, playful, warm and a little pushy, every line a pitch. Clean studio recording."},"olivia":{"voice_id":"3KdkB2LF6PUw0muuS0j7","name":"AoT Olivia","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her late thirties with a quick, bright, articulate American voice. A journalist and mom of two little kids, talks fast, wry and warm, always half distracted. Clean studio recording."},"log":{"voice_id":"DmA9AOv6Fsic2LQdqVVM","name":"AoT Log Lump","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A sleepy cartoon log creature, very slow, deep, woody and drowsy voice, yawning between words, mumbly and content. Animated character voice."},"skeeter":{"voice_id":"3NkCp1SubvPIw3g0s7Rf","name":"AoT Skeeter Swarm","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A cartoon swarm of mosquitoes speaking as one, high-pitched, thin, whiny and buzzy voice with a nasal zzz on every s, nosy and impatient. Animated character voice."},"toad":{"voice_id":"jcb48kKcDpNXjAxnAP2c","name":"AoT Bog Toad","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A huge cartoon toad, deep croaky throaty voice with a rumbling ribbit, territorial and proud, a bit vain. Animated character voice."},"bigone":{"voice_id":"qDteMRfOWoUEc7kcfWvl","name":"AoT The Big One","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An enormous ancient cartoon pond fish, huge slow booming bass voice with gurgling bubbles, pompous and boastful but childlike and easily delighted underneath. Animated character voice."},"washington":{"voice_id":"ARRjeRIXQjOrcraWRDoq","name":"AoT Mr. Washington","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An elderly man in his eighties with a deep, warm, slow voice and a gentle hint of Louisiana in it. A neighborhood storyteller on his porch, unhurried, kind, a little gravelly. Clean studio recording."},"michael":{"voice_id":"24fSFWvKYGI0zVR7L6JQ","name":"AoT Michael","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A tall man in his early forties with a calm, low, dry American voice. A tech dad holding two kids, patient, deadpan, quietly funny, a little tired. Clean studio recording."},"la_woman":{"voice_id":"eLXwnyHT9UJHbuyheJ9m","name":"AoT LA neighbor (woman)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her early thirties with a relaxed, warm, slightly husky Los Angeles voice. Easygoing, wry, a little tired, friendly neighbor energy. Clean studio recording."},"gus":{"voice_id":"CcabrpeMRBXae9HlsCuq","name":"AoT Gus","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An old man in his seventies with a slow, warm, slightly creaky American voice. Deadpan and dignified, treats sitting on a bench like serious athletic training. Unhurried. Clean studio recording."},"mudling":{"voice_id":"E2hOWZ8x3nGJuQURP3SG","name":"AoT Mudling","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A small, silly cartoon creature made of mud, gloopy gurgling voice with wet bubbly consonants, slow and sulky, childlike and a little sad. Animated character voice."},"sal":{"voice_id":"gcJ5PkVgShIxtP5HgbZK","name":"AoT Sal","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his fifties with a thick Long Island New York accent, a slightly nasal, raspy, fast and friendly voice. Chatty taxi driver, warm and a little dramatic, proud of his one cab. Clean studio recording."}});
